  <p>Delivering a rigorous education does not require spending thousands on boxed curriculum packages. Southwest Missouri offers robust low-cost and free educational infrastructure:</p>
  
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Springfield-Greene County Library District:</strong> Beyond literature, access science dissection kits, digital audiobooks, language software, and tech bundles.</li>
    <li><strong>Open-Source Curricula:</strong> Complete, standards-aligned frameworks like AmblesideOnline, Easy Peasy All-in-One, and Core Knowledge Foundation provide free printable lesson plans (K–12).</li>
    <li><strong>Regional Co-ops &amp; Curriculum Swaps:</strong> The 417 homeschool network frequently hosts seasonal book fairs and peer exchanges for low-cost Saxon math sets, lab equipment, and living books.</li>
  </ul>

