    <p>Missouri law mandates four basic records:</p>
    <ol style="color: #3e2723; font-weight: bold; padding-left: 25px;">
      <li><span style="font-weight: normal;">A written record of subjects taught.</span></li>
      <li><span style="font-weight: normal;">A periodic log of hours completed.</span></li>
      <li><span style="font-weight: normal;">Samples of academic work.</span></li>
      <li><span style="font-weight: normal;">An evaluation of academic progress (e.g., portfolio or tests).</span></li>
    </ol>
    
    <p>You do not need expensive software subscriptions to stay compliant. A physical bound ledger or a basic digital spreadsheet tracking <strong>Date</strong>, <strong>Core vs. Non-Core Subject</strong>, <strong>Location</strong>, and <strong>Time Spent</strong> satisfies all statutory requirements.</p>
